ichlet form operator is hypercontractive, Davies and Simon call the Schrödinger operator ``intrinsically hypercontractive\". I will show that if one adds a suitable potential onto an intrinsically hypercontractive Schrödinger operator it remains intrinsically hypercontractive.\nL17: The proof uses a fortuitous relation between the WKB equation and logarithmic Sobolev inequalities. All bounds are dimension independent. The main theorem will be applied to several examples.\nL18: Comments:  | 124 pages, Accepted version\nL19: Subjects:  | Mathematical Physics (math-ph); Functional Analysis (math.FA)\nL20: MSC (Mathematical Subject Classification) classes:  | 81Q15, 47D08 (Primary), 35J10, 35B20, 60J46 (Secondary)\nL21: Cite as:  | 【9†arXiv:2412.20282】 [math-ph]\nL22:    | (or 【10†arXiv:2412.20282v2】 [math-ph] for this version)\nL23:    | 【11†https://doi.org/10.48550/arXiv.2412.20282†doi.org】 arXiv-issued DOI via DataCite\nL24: ## Submission history\nL25: \nL26: From: Leonard Gross [【12†view email】]\nL27: 【5†[v1]】 Sat, 28 Dec 2024 21:42:55 UTC (83 KB)\nL28: [v2] Fri, 23 May 2025 19:57:01 UTC (83 KB)\nL29: \nL30: Full-text links:\nL31: \nL32: ## Access Paper:\nL33: \nL34: View a PDF of the paper titled Invariance of intrinsic hypercontractivity under perturbation of Schr\\\"odinger operators, by Leonard Gross\nL35: \nL36:   * 【7†View PDF】\nL37:   * 【8†HTML (experimental)】\nL38:   * 【13†TeX Source】\nL39: \nL40: 【14†view license】\nL41: ### Current browse context:\nL42: \nL43: math-ph\nL44: \nL45: 【15†< prev】   |   【16†next >】\nL46: \nL47: 【17†new】 | 【18†recent】 | 【19†2024-12】\nL48: \nL49: Change to browse by:\nL50: \nL51: 【20†math】\nL52: 【21†math.FA】\nL53: 【22†math.MP】\nL54: \nL55: ### References & Citations\nL56: \nL57:   * 【23†SciX†scixplorer.org】\nL58:   * 【24†Google Scholar†scholar.google.com】\nL59:   * 【25†Semantic Scholar†api.semanticscholar.org】\nL60: \nL61: [Button: export BibTeX citation] Loading...\nL62: \nL63: ## BibTeX formatted citation\nL64: \nL65: [Button: ×